`Exec` returns a `CommandTag`; check `tag.RowsAffected()`. Zero rows → the id didn't exist → return 404 (not 500, not a silent 204). One row → 204 No Content. A DELETE that matched nothing is not an error to the DB, so you must surface the distinction yourself:

```go
tag, err := pool.Exec(ctx, `DELETE FROM bookmarks WHERE id=$1`, id)
if err != nil { return err }
if tag.RowsAffected() == 0 { return ErrNotFound }
```
